{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_53", "type": "agent_message", "text": "Note creation with the reversed card model produced two cards, editing survived reopening, and discarding an unsaved edit kept the saved value. I also tested the due-date range’s empty, reversed, equal, and rotated states; setting a two-day range changed the selected card’s due date as expected, and I undid it to restore the starting schedule. Next I’m checking deck-management persistence and the statistics screens."}}
